      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KENMARE BAY (2) arrives off a good win at Rosehill when well backed. Has good form all around this trip without specifically tackling it, though doubt that should worry. Expect him to stalk them into the lane and be too strong late. TARAVIA (7) is a danger, having only been collared on the line by CAPTAIN MAVERICK two weeks ago, who he now meets with a good pull at the weights. Thompson sticks and looks the one they'll need to reel in. CAPTAIN MAVERICK (1) has done little wrong this campaign and silenced his doubters last start when arriving just in time. Bit tougher now up in the weights but he nevertheless he deserves respect. BARAZIN (3) has to turn around that Eagle Farm result, but a pull at the weights gives him a chance. SAMURAI WARRIOR (5) was a sharp improver at the Sunny Coast third-up and looks even better suited stretching to this trip on the short turnaround. Can fill the drum at a nice quote.",
